@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `hvac-nouns`
IMPORT `hvac-law-s6-second-schedule`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`

-- hvac-law-s8-validity.l4 -- Law s 8: the validity of a licence and its renewal.
-- Quoted from Hebrew Wikisource rev 2947808 (unofficial); the gazette (Sefer HaChukim 3349
-- p. 184) has the same words.
--
-- THE COUNTING.  As first encoded, the convention for every period was a fork (F-D4): a period
-- of N years or days measured "from" a day does not count that day and ends on the day N later.
-- Interpretation Law 5741-1981 states it: s 10(a) (days and weeks "from" a day: that day is not
-- counted) and s 10(b) (months and years "after" an event end on the day with the event day's
-- number, or the month's last day, inside the period), and s 8 makes "until 31 March" include
-- the day named.  The five-year limb below goes through il-interpretation-time.l4, the
-- Interpretation row's module, vendored unchanged.
--
-- s 10(c) (a rest day does not end a period) is NOT applied to a licence's period of validity
-- (fork F-X2).  (c) protects the time in which an act must be done from losing its last working
-- days; validity is how long an entitlement lasts, and nothing has to be done on its last day.
-- The "31 March" limb is a date, not a counted period, so (c) could never reach it.  The
-- function marked "if s 10(c) applied" shows the other reading.
-- A licence is valid from the day it is given although s 10 does not count that day in the
-- five years (fork F-V4).

§ `Section 8: The validity of a licence and its renewal`

@@Q law 100@@

-- THE FORK IN s 8 (F-V1).  "עד 31 במרץ של השנה החמישית מהשנה שבה ניתן הרישיון": the fifth year
-- from the year of the grant.  Is the year of the grant counted as year 0, or as year 1?
--   A (taken):  year 0.  A licence given in 2025 runs to 31 March 2030 at the latest.
--   B:          year 1.  A licence given in 2025 runs to 31 March 2029 at the latest.
-- A is taken because under B the five-year limb could never be the earlier one: 31 March of
-- the fourth year after the grant is always earlier than the fifth anniversary of any day in
-- the grant year, so "לפי המוקדם" (whichever is earlier) would have nothing to choose between.
-- Under A the five-year limb wins exactly for a grant between 1 January and 30 March.  Reading B
-- is kept as its own function so the difference can be tested.

@ref Law s 8, "חמש שנים"; Interpretation Law s 10(b)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of the five-year limb for a period beginning on` d MEANS
    `s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 5 `years after an event on` d

-- The five-year limb if s 10(c) were applied: it does not end on a day of rest.
@ref Law s 8, "חמש שנים"; Interpretation Law s 10(b), (c)
GIVEN d    IS A DATE
      rest IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of the five-year limb for a period beginning on` d `, if s 10(c) applied to a period of validity, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest MEANS
    `s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` 5 `years after an event on` d `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest

@ref Law s 8, "עד 31 במרץ של השנה החמישית מהשנה שבה ניתן הרישיון", reading A
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the 31 March limb for a licence given on` d MEANS
    YMD ((DATE_YEAR d) PLUS 5) 3 31

@ref Law s 8, "עד 31 במרץ של השנה החמישית מהשנה שבה ניתן הרישיון", reading B
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the 31 March limb on the other reading for a licence given on` d MEANS
    YMD ((DATE_YEAR d) PLUS 4) 3 31

@ref Law s 8: "לפי המוקדם"
GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier of` a `and` b MEANS
    IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

@ref Law s 8, "לפי המוקדם", reading A
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the first validity period of a licence given on` d MEANS
    `the earlier of`
        (`the end of the five-year limb for a period beginning on` d)
        `and`
        (`the 31 March limb for a licence given on` d)

@ref Law s 8, "לפי המוקדם", reading B
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the first validity period on the other reading, for a licence given on` d MEANS
    `the earlier of`
        (`the end of the five-year limb for a period beginning on` d)
        `and`
        (`the 31 March limb on the other reading for a licence given on` d)

-- The first validity period if s 10(c) were applied to its five-year limb (reading A of F-V1).
@ref Law s 8, "לפי המוקדם", reading A; Interpretation Law s 10(b), (c)
GIVEN d    IS A DATE
      rest IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the first validity period of a licence given on` d `, if s 10(c) applied to a period of validity, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest MEANS
    `the earlier of`
        (`the end of the five-year limb for a period beginning on` d `, if s 10(c) applied to a period of validity, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest)
        `and`
        (`the 31 March limb for a licence given on` d)

-- THE GAP IN s 8 (F-V2).  A licence "can be renewed for additional validity periods", and a
-- "validity period" is defined by the formula above, which runs from "the year in which the
-- licence was given".  A renewed licence was not given again.  Whether the next period starts
-- when the old one ends or when the renewal is granted, and which year the "fifth year" is
-- counted from, the text does not say.  The encoding does not borrow the first-period formula.
@ref Law s 8: "וניתן לחדשו לתקופות תוקף נוספות"
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of a renewed validity period` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 8 says a licence can be renewed for additional validity periods but does not say when a renewed period starts or which year its 'fifth year' is counted from"

-- The last day of the licence's validity period as it now stands.  A temporary licence for
-- a foreign expert (s 9) runs for the period it was given for.
@ref Law s 8; s 9(a)
GIVEN l IS A Licence
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the validity period of` l MEANS
    BRANCH IF l's `a temporary licence for a foreign expert`
           THEN CONSIDER l's `the last day of a temporary licence`
                WHEN JUST x  THEN x
                WHEN NOTHING THEN REFUSE "a temporary licence's last day must be supplied: section 9 fixes only a ceiling of one year per period"
           IF l's `the current validity period is a renewal`
           THEN `the end of a renewed validity period`
           OTHERWISE `the last day of the first validity period of a licence given on` (l's `the day the validity period began`)

@ref Law s 8; Interpretation Law s 8 ("עד" includes the day named)
GIVEN l IS A Licence
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the licence` l `is valid on` d MEANS
        d AT LEAST l's `the day the validity period began`
    AND `s 8 — the date` d `is up to and including` (`the last day of the validity period of` l)

-- The conditions for renewal are those of s 6 except (a)(4).
@ref Law s 8: "בהתקיים התנאים לפי סעיף 6, למעט התנאי לפי סעיף קטן (א)(4) של אותו סעיף"
GIVEN a IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8: the conditions for renewing a licence are met by` a MEANS
    `s 6(a)(1) to (3): the conditions for renewing a licence are met by` a
